---
title: Crab and Fennel Spaghetti
servings: 2
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Easy
cuisine: Italian
---

Put a #large non-stick frying pan{} on a medium-low heat. Trim the @fennel{1%bulb}, pick and reserve any leafy tops, then halve the bulb and finely slice it. Place in the pan with @olive oil{1%tbsp} and cook with the lid on for ~{5%minutes}. Meanwhile cook the @dried spaghetti{150%g} in a pan of boiling salted water, then drain.

Deseed and finely slice the @red chillies{2}, stir into the fennel pan and cook uncovered until soft and sticky, stirring occasionally. Halve the @cherry tomatoes{160%g}(mixed colours) and toss into the pan for ~{2%minutes}, followed by the @crabmeat{160%g}(mixed brown and white) for ~{1%minute}, and finally the drained pasta.

Drizzle with @olive oil{}, season with @sea salt{} and @black pepper{}(freshly ground), top with any reserved fennel tops, and dust with @parmesan{}(grated).